#!/bin/bash
# flatpak stub. Logs every call to $LOGS/flatpak. User installs are listed in
# $LOGS/flatpak-installed and remotes in $LOGS/flatpak-remotes. install
# exports a desktop entry the way Flatpak does, under
# ${XDG_DATA_HOME:-~/.local/share}/flatpak/exports/share/applications/.
printf '%s\n' "$*" >>"$LOGS/flatpak"
inst=$LOGS/flatpak-installed
remotes=$LOGS/flatpak-remotes
touch "$inst" "$remotes"
data=${XDG_DATA_HOME:-$HOME/.local/share}
last=${!#}
case ${1:-} in
  info)
    grep -qxF -- "$last" "$inst"
    ;;
  remote-list)
    cat "$remotes"
    ;;
  remote-add)
    grep -qx flathub "$remotes" || echo flathub >>"$remotes"
    ;;
  install)
    echo "$last" >>"$inst"
    mkdir -p "$data/flatpak/exports/share/applications"
    printf '[Desktop Entry]\nName=Test App\nExec=/usr/bin/flatpak run %s\nNotShowIn=KDE;\nX-Flatpak=%s\n\n[Desktop Action new-window]\nName=New Window\nOnlyShowIn=GNOME;\n' \
      "$last" "$last" >"$data/flatpak/exports/share/applications/$last.desktop"
    ;;
  uninstall)
    grep -vxF -- "$last" "$inst" >"$inst.new" || true
    mv "$inst.new" "$inst"
    ;;
  *)
    exit 1
    ;;
esac
